    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround\n\n### Description\n\nCurrently, the cursor will move to opening bracket after the operation on the surrounding. I think this is a bit counterintuitive and most time I have to move back to the original char.\r\n\r\nIllustration (`*` is cursor)\r\n\r\n| Key  | Line            | Delete        | Replace         |\r\n| ---- | --------------- | ------------- | --------------- |\r\n| `)`  | `!( *a (bb) )!` | `! *a (bb) !` | `(( *a (bb) ))` |\r\n\r\nThe cases about cross lines and the original position on bracket may need to be handled specially.",
    "closed_at": "2023-02-13T10:31:38Z",
