        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for suggestion!\r\n\r\nI've thought about it several times already. There are two main reasons for this behavior:\r\n- \"Preserving\" cursor usually means additional (not trivial) computations because text usually changes.\r\n- It is a default Neovim behavior for operators. See [docs about operators](https://neovim.io/doc/user/motion.html#operator): \"After applying the operator the cursor is mostly left at the start of the text that was operated upon.\".\r\n\r\nLet this be open for a while, but I doubt this will change.",
