        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> * \"Preserving\" cursor usually means additional (not trivial) computations because text usually changes.\r\n> * It is a default Neovim behavior for operators. See [docs about operators](https://neovim.io/doc/user/motion.html#operator): \"After applying the operator the cursor is mostly left at the start of the text that was operated upon.\".\r\n\r\n(I thought this seemed better here given context, but I can start a new issue if preferred.)\r\n\r\nHey, thanks for your work on all the `mini.nvim` plugins.\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to (have an option to) have the final position for cursor be the start of the left-hand surround text.\r\n\r\nCurrent behaviour:\r\n```\r\nBefore:\r\nsome_statement\r\n  ^\r\nAfter saiw:\r\n(some_statement)\r\n ^\r\n```\r\n\r\nMy preferred behaviour:\r\n```\r\nBefore:\r\nsome_statement\r\n  ^\r\nAfter saiw:\r\n(some_statement)\r\n^\r\n```\r\n\r\nSome justification:\r\n- This was the default behaviour with `tpope/vim-surround`\r\n- It's particularly useful because the typical case is to have an expression, wrap it in parens, then insert `if` or `function_call` etc before the first paren. The current behaviour requires extra movement before doing so.\r\n- It's reasonable to include the added surrounds within the definition of \"the text that was operated upon\", at which point my suggested behaviour is the natural consequence.\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\nAndrew",
            "created_at": "2023-12-17T12:21:20Z",
