        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for kind words!\r\n\r\n> Current behaviour:\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> Before:\r\n> some_statement\r\n>   ^\r\n> After saiw:\r\n> (some_statement)\r\n>  ^\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nThe current behavior is most certainly the preferred way because it enables dot-repeat on the same textobject.\r\n\r\nAlthough the suggested behavior is useful for adding `if` before it, there are other use cases which benefit from current behavior. For example, wrapping in function call with `saiwf` and then prepend arguments inside the parenthesis.\r\n\r\n> * It's reasonable to include the added surrounds within the definition of \"the text that was operated upon\", at which point my suggested behaviour is the natural consequence.\r\n\r\nI don't think it is reasonable to include added surrounds, as they are the result of operation on the text that was operated upon.",
